From 48fc243ce353722d38d09f85a9ae45a44fff4a54 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: iam <iam@iashur.internal>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 06:14:20 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] input: legacy state coexists with action manifests + menu
 passes through to games

Two structural fixes from docs/49's diagnosis (the Blade Runner 9732 case:
pose works, every button dead):

1) InputSessionData held a single OnceLock<LoadedActions> enum (Legacy XOR
Manifest) -- structurally nowhere to serve legacy state once a manifest
loaded, and get_legacy_controller_state hard-returned false forever. Now
two independent slots; the legacy set is created idempotently and attached
IN THE SAME attach_action_sets call as the manifest's sets (OpenXR's
call-once constraint), synced every frame. Real SteamVR tolerates titles
mixing both APIs -- now so do we. Bonus discovery: check_system_recenter_hold
was only reachable from the legacy-only branch, so the hold-3s recenter
(patch 0001) was silently dead in every manifest title -- now runs always.

2) The Windows/menu buttons were consumed exclusively by the recenter
shortcut, never surfacing to games (docs/49: SUPERHOT's dead menu class).
Short presses now pass through via EVRButtonId::System (advertised in every
profile's mask, never populated before); the instant a 3s hold fires
recenter, the exposed value force-clears the same frame.

84 unit + 1 integration tests pass (2 added, 2 updated that pinned the old
buggy exclusive model).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
